# GitHub language statistics (Linguist).
#
# Linguist measures bytes per language, not the value of the code. The Spec Kit tooling that
# lives next to the product (.specify scripts and templates, the generated agent commands) and
# the artifacts it renders (feature specs, architecture renderings) dwarf the C# sources, so the
# language bar reported the tooling's languages instead of C#. These files stay in the repository
# and in the file tree; they are only taken out of the language statistics.
#
#   linguist-vendored       installed/third-party tooling that is copied into the repository
#   linguist-documentation  prose and generated artifacts, never product code
#
# Verify with: git check-attr linguist-vendored linguist-documentation -- <path>
.specify/**      linguist-vendored
.clinerules/**   linguist-vendored
specs/**         linguist-documentation

# Already detected as documentation by Linguist's own heuristic (docs/, doc/); stated
# explicitly so the statistics do not depend on heuristic changes.
docs/**          linguist-documentation
